.TH BINGUX-EFFECTS 1 "2026-10-28" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-effects \- sound effects engine for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-effects run
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects restore
.br
.B bingux-effects render
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects presets
.RB { output | input }
.br
.B bingux-effects scan
.br
.B bingux-effects import
.I FILE
.RB { output | input }
.RI [ NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-effects
puts a chain of audio plugins between applications and the speakers
.RB ( output )
or between a microphone and applications
.RB ( input ).
It runs each effect of the active preset as a PipeWire
.B filter-chain
in a PipeWire client process of its own and joins them with links, so an effect
can be added, removed, switched off or moved without the others stopping.
There is one such stack for each direction.
It creates a virtual device (\(lqEffects (Output)\(rq or \(lqEffects (Input)\(rq),
makes it the default device and sends the result to the real device.
When it stops, the real device is the default again.
.PP
Bingux Settings, under Sound, Effects, edits the presets and turns the effects
on and off.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "run " DIRECTION
Run one direction until stopped. The user unit
.B bingux-effects@output.service
does this.
.TP
.B restore
Start each direction that Settings has turned on. Run it at login.
.TP
.BI "render " DIRECTION
Print the filter-chain configuration of every stage of the active preset.
.TP
.BI "reload " DIRECTION
Tell the running engine to read the preset again and change only what differs.
Settings does this after every edit; it starts the engine if it is not running.
.TP
.BI "status " DIRECTION
Print what the running engine reports for each effect, as JSON.
.TP
.BI "presets " DIRECTION
List the presets.
.TP
.B scan
List the plugins found for the effects Bingux offers, as JSON.
.TP
.BI "import " "FILE DIRECTION " [ NAME ]
Read an EasyEffects, Equalizer APO or AutoEq preset and save it as a Bingux preset.
.SH PLUGINS
The effects are the published plugins that Easy Effects hosts: Linux Studio
Plugins (equalizer, compressor, limiter, gate, expander, multiband compressor
and gate, filter, delay, loudness, auto gain), Calf Studio Gear (bass
enhancer, exciter, crusher, de-esser, reverb, stereo tools), ZamAudio
(maximizer), MDA (bass loudness), x42 (autotune), Rubber Band (pitch) and
PipeWire's own convolver.
LV2 plugins need PipeWire's LV2 loader and are looked for in
.BR LV2_PATH ,
.I ~/.lv2
and the usual system directories; Rubber Band is a LADSPA plugin and is looked
for in
.BR LADSPA_PATH
and the usual directories.
The package of each plugin is named by the effect's page in Settings when it is
missing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LV2_PATH
Where to look for LV2 plugins, instead of the usual directories.
.TP
.B LADSPA_PATH
Where to look for LADSPA libraries, instead of the usual directories.
.TP
.B BINGUX_EFFECTS_BIN
The
.B bingux-effects
program that Settings starts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/effects/state.json
What is on, the preset and the device.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/effects/{output,input}/presets/NAME.json
One preset per file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bingux/effects/plugins.json
The plugin scan, cached by file date.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bingux/effects/
The generated configuration, process id and level meters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/audio-effects.md in the Bingux source.
